<section class="section" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Stadium and venue retail questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does the POS work when stadium Wi-Fi goes down?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Store-and-Forward technology keeps every terminal fully operational during network outages. Transactions are encrypted and stored locally on the device, then automatically synced to the cloud back office once connectivity is restored. During the halftime rush at a sold-out game, this means zero lost sales even when 50,000 fans saturate the network.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Does Teamwork Commerce handle food & beverage or merchandise?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce specializes in merchandise retail, team jerseys, hats, memorabilia, and fan gear. For F&B operations, Teamwork integrates with your existing concession POS or F&B vendor via open APIs. Unifying food and merchandise under one platform is the long-term goal, and Teamwork's open architecture is built to support that integration.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How quickly can seasonal staff learn the system?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The Colorado Rockies put new associates on registers in five minutes after they start. The iOS interface follows familiar design patterns that most people already know. For stadium retail where staff might work 20 games a year, this virtually eliminates training overhead.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does this compare to stadium-merchandise-only POS systems?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce covers the whole retail fleet, not just the stadium store. retailcloud focuses primarily on stadium merchandise with 70+ venue deployments. Teamwork Commerce offers a broader platform: native end-to-end RFID (not third-party), Store-and-Forward offline resilience (critical for network-saturated venues), integrated OMS with Endless Aisle and ship-from-store, real-time AI fan loyalty via the LAVA partnership, and the full omnichannel stack (BOPIS, BORIS, cross-channel inventory). For venues that also operate standalone retail stores, like InnovaSport's 250 locations, Teamwork scales from the stadium to the entire retail fleet on one platform.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What fan spending data is available?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The cloud back office provides sales analytics by game period (pre-game, halftime, post-game), per-fan average spend, terminal performance, product velocity, and inventory turnover. Industry data shows 77% of fans say they would buy more if queues were shorter, 53% wait 15 minutes or more at concession stands, and venues offering mobile ordering see per-capita spend rise 22%.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Which stadiums and venues use Teamwork Commerce?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce powers stadium and venue retail for the Colorado Rockies, Milwaukee Bucks, InnovaSport (250 stores across Mexico), and Sports Basement. The LAVA loyalty integration is live with NFL teams. The platform handles large bursts of sales volume with offline resilience, RFID self-checkout, and rapid seasonal staff deployment.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
